<title>GERMANY: Bank says recommends German export-senstive stocks.</title>
<headline>Bank says recommends German export-senstive stocks.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Berenberg Bank said on Friday that it was recommending investors with a long-term outlook consider German export-sensitive stocks due to the dollar rising above 1.50 marks.</p>
<p>The bank specifically recommended pharmaceuticals group Schering AG, chemical and drugs group BASF AG and industrial group Daimler-Benz AG.</p>
<p>It also recommended investors consider cyclical stocks.</p>
<p>But the Hamburg-based bank said it recommended investors a neutral position in bank and insurance stocks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
